+# Delivery - Mosaic3D readout failure: Method B + inference diagnosis
+
+## One-line conclusion (a/b/c)
+As of this session Method B is **not yet closed**: (a) fg-mIoU > 0.17573 — NOT met
+(epoch-1 B = 0.1273 < baseline 0.15475, rising); (b) cos(d_vis,d_txt) pull-back — PENDING
+final-ckpt eval; (c) gain on sibling pairs — PENDING. The **firmly established** result is
+that annotation-free *inference-time* readout cannot fix the sibling naming (dead-knot);
+the only realized gain is the `mask_text_vote` instance-consistency axis (**+0.02098**).
+
+## What is proven now (offline, GPU-free, self-checked口径 fg-mIoU=0.15475 OK)
+- TASK2: separation is easy, naming is the wall. Unsupervised 2-means + oracle naming reaches
+  instance acc 0.62 (vs baseline 0.452), but every annotation-free naming (anchor_decorrelate,
+  caption_proto, unsup text-naming) is <= baseline. `anchor_decorrelate` and `caption_proto`
+  are negative results. Pre-registered criterion ① CONFIRMED, ② NOT met.
+- TASK3: `pred_masks` are Segment3D (mask!=GT-inst in 302/312 scenes, per-mask scores), so
+  mask consistency is annotation-free; mask_text_vote is a consistency axis (not a direction fix).
+- Task0 ceilings reproduced exactly: top25=0.1906, top50=0.2118, all=0.3257.
+
+## What is pending (GPU-gated by the mandated 128-epoch run; auto-runs via watcher)
+- TASK1 three-tier eval of the final B ckpt: B / B+mask_text_vote / B+anchor_decorrelate, with
+  fg-mIoU/mAP deltas, and the cos mechanism check. Handled by `scripts/phase4_autoeval.sh`
+  (fires only when a GPU is genuinely free or training ends; results -> `method_b_autoeval/summary.txt`).
+
+## Reports
+- `readout_inference_diag.md` (TASK2), `axes_summary.md` (TASK3), `method_b.md` (TASK1),
+  `oracle_real_labelspace.md` (Task0), `task2/` (clusters + per-mode JSON + per-cluster).
+
+## Iron-rule compliance
+Annotation-free throughout (no ScanNet200 GT in any method; GT only for scoring/oracle);
+instance grouping for methods uses Segment3D masks; fixed scoring口径 with baseline self-check;
+pre-registered criteria fixed before running; no unsupported success claimed.
